<div id="2026-11-10-barcode-inventory-api" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-10 — Phone barcode scan: inventory lookup, product facts, and photo</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> New session-gated routes for the Android scan flow: <code>GET /api/inventory/item/by_barcode</code>, <code>GET /api/inventory/product_lookup</code>, <code>GET/POST /api/inventory/item/ency_links</code>, and <code>POST /api/inventory/photo/upload</code>. Item create now checks barcode before SKU and says <code>existing</code> / <code>matched_on</code> instead of pretending a barcode hit was created. Item update accepts barcode, product, and ingredients. <code>GET /api/inventory/items</code> now includes barcode, notes, image, and prices, and can filter by barcode or category. <code>?sitename=</code> on that list is honoured only for a CSC admin.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The phone can scan a code, but the server had no session-gated lookup, no Open Food Facts fallback, and no item-photo path. Barcode was also looked up with <code>find</code> even though it is not unique.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Schema Compare.</strong> <code>hk_item_product</code> needs two new columns from the Result file: <code>ingredients_text</code> (TEXT) and <code>ingredients_source</code> (VARCHAR 32). No SQL was applied. Until those columns exist, ingredient reads return an empty list and <code>missing</code> includes <code>ingredients_schema</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Controller/Api.pm</code>, <code>Controller/Inventory.pm</code>, <code>Util/HealthKitchen.pm</code>, <code>Util/ProductLookup.pm</code>, <code>Util/ItemImage.pm</code>, <code>Util/InventoryBarcode.pm</code>, <code>Result/HealthKitchen/ItemProduct.pm</code>.</p>
</div>
